From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:12:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] fix(kanban): a worker stop request ends the run as one
 native block; read-loop family halt

Two local additions (RHOAI3 V16-3).

Worker stop request. The dispatcher gives every worker run a per-run,
initially absent path in HERMES_KANBAN_STOP_REQUEST
(<board>/stop-requests/<task>.run<id>.json). A tool the worker runs may
create it with {"kind": "needs_input"|"capability", "reason": ...}. After
that tool result the runtime records the native block once, bound to the
run (kanban_db.block_task with expected_run_id, plus a
worker_stop_request event), refuses every later tool call in the batch
and ends the turn before another model request. Files on disk are not
touched. A resumed run (after unblock) has a new run id and path.

Read-only log context search family. Same tool, same workdir and the
same read-only command once only grep's context-size options (-A/-B/-C,
-NUM and the long forms) are removed form one family. A read that shows
an output line the family has not shown is progress; five reads in a
row that show nothing new halt with read_family_no_new_content_halt,
naming the family. Any other number, pattern, file or option is a
different family; an evidence-changing call (write, patch, code
execution, a non-read-only command) resets the families. The
identical-call guard is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
